# Simulation Blueprint Engine
Author: C. MATTHEW BLACKWELL — Independent Designer

## Overview
The Simulation Blueprint Engine is a modular physics and constraint‑driven
numerical simulation framework. It models engineered systems under:

- thermal limits
- material fatigue
- power budgets
- plasma instabilities
- vacuum chamber boundaries

Each simulation run is sealed with cryptographic provenance to ensure
tamper‑evident integrity.

## Features
- Modular physics subsystems (thermal, structural, power, plasma, environment)
- Global constraint manager with violation detection
- Deterministic integrator loop
- Encrypted run records (hash + signature)
- CLI interface for simulation, validation, and reporting
- Optional GUI dashboard for visualization

## Directory Structure
See `/simulation_blueprint/` for full module layout.

## Running a Simulation

python cli/main.py simulate --config scenarios/example_scenario.json


## Validating a Run

python cli/main.py validate-run --input sealed_record.json


## Extending the Engine
Add new physics modules under `/physics/`.

